From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] combase: an interface's proxy/stub class registered for the user is found

OneDrive installs for the user and registers its interfaces' proxy/stub classes under HKCU\Software\Classes\Interface. CoGetPSClsid looked at the machine's registrations only, so its FileCoAuth server could not marshal IFileCoAuthNotify back to OneDrive (E_NOINTERFACE, an RPC fault). The user's registration now comes first, as for classes; an elevated process still uses the machine's alone.
---
diff --git a/dlls/combase/combase.c b/dlls/combase/combase.c
index f12fa98..74db07d 100644
--- a/dlls/combase/combase.c
+++ b/dlls/combase/combase.c
@@ -2562,7 +2562,9 @@ static HRESULT get_ps_clsid_from_registry(const WCHAR* path, REGSAM access, CLSI
 
     access |= KEY_READ;
 
-    if (open_classes_key(HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT, path, access, &hkey))
+    /* an interface registered for the user (a per-user install's proxies) comes first, as for classes */
+    if (open_user_classes_key(path, NULL, access, &hkey) &&
+        open_classes_key(HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT, path, access, &hkey))
         return REGDB_E_IIDNOTREG;
 
     len = sizeof(value);
